All 625 cases pass and `verify.js` confirms the fix is legitimate.

The bug: `orderTotal()` in `src/pricing.js` was computing tax on the pre-discount amount instead of the discounted amount, even though its own comment said tax should apply to "what's actually owed." Fixed by taxing the discounted total instead:

```js
function orderTotal(cents, discountPct, taxRate) {
  const discounted = applyDiscount(cents, discountPct);
  return applyTax(discounted, taxRate);
}
```

This only showed up in rows where both a discount and a tax were non-zero, which is why most of the suite looked fine and only a handful of cases in "order totals" were actually failing.
